<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'woman' through the use of first-person pronouns in the text ('in my country', 'here in other countries i am also free...'). The text explicitly maps the speaker's personal experience and perspective onto the visual representation of the woman, making her the embodiment of 'me' in the meme's narrative. This projection is reinforced by the analogical mapping where the woman serves as the instantiation of the speaker 'me'."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#perspectiveAlignedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text following the perspective, depth, and vanishing points of memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DimensionsInterrelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relationships and interactions between different meme dimensions"@en .
