<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman wearing a headscarf (a hijab), with text overlay stating that in her country, wearing it is common and optional, but in other countries, she is also free to wear it if she wants. The scene is neutral, showing the woman in a casual setting, possibly a café, with no overtly harmful or abusive visual elements. The overall intent is to convey a message of personal freedom and cultural relativism regarding religious attire. There is no toxicity present, as the text does not attack, disparage, or stereotype any group. The meme uses juxtaposition to highlight the contrast between cultural norms and personal choice, promoting tolerance and individual autonomy. The visual elements (headscarf, clothing, setting) are presented without exaggeration or harmful context, and the text is factual and non-misleading. The intent is to normalize the choice to wear religious attire across different cultural contexts, without promoting any harmful or hateful message."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#situationallyIronicalTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#contradicts> .
