<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#underpinsCosmicIronyOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text highlighting the absurdity or ironic nature of the visual situation in memes"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The woman is mapped as 'me' in the context of her personal freedom regarding the hijab."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#complementaryTo> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#OverallIntent> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Overall Intent elements from the image. Overall Intent includes: communicative purposes, creator intentions, message goals, intended effects, purpose indicators, and intent signals. For each intentional element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'humor_intent', 'social_commentary'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the humor intent', 'the social commentary'), 3) A brief description of the intended purpose or effect. Focus on what the meme creator likely intended to communicate or achieve. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"humor_intent\", \"label\": \"the humor intent\", \"description\": \"The meme appears designed to create humor through the contrast between the girl's calm expression and the chaotic fire scene\"}"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#cultural_differences> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The variations in beliefs, practices, and norms between different cultures. The meme highlights the contrast between the cultural context of the woman's home country and other countries, emphasizing that cultural differences should not be used to restrict personal freedoms."@en .
