<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#pointingAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text positioned to point at or direct attention to specific elements in memes"@en .
_:nc16d0f36373e49da9b4619e02a33496ab54 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#assertion_about_01472> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#mapping_1> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#modesty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The quality of being reserved or restrained in behavior or dress, often associated with religious or cultural practices. The hijab is a symbol of modesty, and the meme implies that the woman's choice to wear it is a personal expression of modesty, not a requirement imposed by others."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#selectivelyMasking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates strategic placement of text to selectively hide or reveal specific content in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semanticallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "semantically adjacent to"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#narrativeFlowAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "narrative flow adjacent to"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#verballyIronicalTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "verbally ironical to"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#neutral_calmness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The woman in the image has a composed, neutral facial expression with direct eye contact and a relaxed posture. Her expression conveys calmness and self-assurance, without any overt emotional display such as joy, sadness, or anger. This neutrality aligns with the message of the text, which emphasizes personal freedom and non-confrontational acceptance of cultural differences."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#global_citizenship> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "global citizenship"@en .
